D A DEFINITIVE AGREEMENT TO ACQUIRE AZTECA SYSTEMS, LLC ON SEPTEMBER 30, 2019. IN ADDITION, THE ACQUISITION WILL ENABLE CITYWORKS TO LEVERAGE TRIMBLE'S GLOBAL FOOTPRINT IN MULTIPLE INDUSTRIES. THE CITYWORKS BUSINESS WILL BE REPORTED AS PART OF TRIMBLE'S RESOURCES AND UTILITIES SEGMENT. THE TRANSACTION IS SUBJECTED TO CUSTOMARY CLOSING CONDITIONS AND EXPIRATION OF THE WAITING PERIOD UNDER THE HART-SCOTT-RODINO ANTITRUST IMPROVEMENTS ACT. AS OF OCTOBER 11, 2019, FEDERAL TRADE COMMISSION HAS GRANTED THE EARLY TERMINATION OF ANTITRUST APPROVAL WAITING PERIOD UNDER THE HART-SCOTT-RODINO ANTITRUST IMPROVEMENTS ACT. THE TRANSACTION IS EXPECTED TO CLOSE IN THE FOURTH QUARTER OF 2019. MATTHEW GEMELLO, ERIC WALL,\xa0HARI RAMAN,\xa0DIANA GILLIS AND JULIANO BANUELOS OF ORRICK, HERRINGTON & SUTCLIFFE LLP ACTED AS LEGAL ADVISOR TO TRIMBLE IN THE TRANSACTION.\n"}{'symbol': 'TYL', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES LAUNCHES CLOUD-BASED LAW ENFORCEMENT ANALYTICS SOLUTION', 'text': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES, INC. ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS LAUNCHED ITS SOCRATA-BASED CLOUD APPLICATION, LAW ENFORCEMENT ANALYTICS, A NEW DATA-RICH PRODUCT FOR PUBLIC SAFETY COMMAND STAFF. THE EASY TO READ DASHBOARD OF THE LAW ENFORCEMENT ANALYTICS SOLUTION SHOWS COMPARISON OF CRIME TYPES YEAR OVER YEAR. LAW ENFORCEMENT ANALYTICS ALLOWS PUBLIC SAFETY STAFF TO HAVE A COMPREHENSIVE VIEW INTO CRIME STATISTICS IN THEIR COMMUNITY. WITH THE TOOL, THEY CAN IDENTIFY TYPES OF CRIME THAT HAVE INCREASED OR DECREASED IN A GIVEN AREA, DETERMINE AND VISUALIZE WHERE CRIMES OCCURRED, AND PINPOINT WHEN CRIME TYPES OCCUR MOST FREQUENTLY. THIS INFORMATION ALLOWS LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES TO CREATE SPECIFIC PLANS OR TACTICS IN A CERTAIN REGION, FOR A SPECIFIC CRIME TYPE, OR OVER A GIVEN TIMEFRAME. THE SOLUTION PROVIDES A VISUAL REPRESENTATION FOR COMMAND STAFF THAT SUMMARIZES CRIMES ACROSS POLICE BEATS ANDSECTORS, ALLOWING USERS TO VIEW ALL ACTIVE TACTICS IN THE AREA. THE INFORMATION ENABLES AGENCIES TO; ADDRESS CRIME PATTERNS BY DEFINING AND IMPROVING TACTICS, SHOW THE IMPACT OF TACTICS ON CRIME VIA DASHBOARDS, REDUCE TIME SPENT PREPARING STATISTICAL REPORTS AND ALLEVIATE RESOURCES AND MANAGE MULTIPLE IMPROVEMENT INITIATIVES.'}{'symbol': 'TYL', 'date': '2019-10-02 10:30:00', 'title': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES SAYS IT HAS ENTERED INTO A NEW FIVE-YEAR $400 MLN UNSECURED REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY', 'text': "TYLER TECHNOLOGIES ANNOUNCES EXPANDED REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY.TYLER TECHNOLOGIES INC - IT HAS ENTERED INTO A NEW FIVE-YEAR, $400 MILLION UNSECURED REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY.TYLER TECHNOLOGIES INC - NEW CREDIT FACILITY REPLACES TYLER'S EXISTING $300 MILLION SECURED CREDIT FACILITY, WHICH WAS SCHEDULED TO MATURE IN NOV 2020.TYLER TECHNOLOGIES - IN ADDITION TO $400 MILLION FACILITY, NEW CREDIT FACILITY ALSO PROVIDES A MINIMUM OF $250 MILLION OF ADDITIONAL UNCOMMITTED FUNDING."}{'symbol': 'UDR', 'date': '2019-10-02 19:30:00', 'title': 'UDR PRICES $100 MILLION OF 3.200% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE 2030', 'text': 'UDR PRICES $100 MILLION OF 3.200% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE 2030 AND $300 MILLION OF 3.100% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE 2034 AND ANNOUNCES REDEMPTION OF ALL OUTSTANDING 4.625% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE JANUARY 2022.UDR - PRICED OFFERING OF $100 MILLION 3.200% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE 2030 & $300 MILLION 3.100% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE 2034.UDR INC - 2030 NOTES WERE PRICED AT 103.319% OF PRINCIPAL AMOUNT, PLUS ACCRUED INTEREST FROM JULY 2, 2019 TO YIELD 2.817% TO MATURITY.UDR INC - 2034 NOTES WERE PRICED AT 99.557% OF PRINCIPAL AMOUNT, PLUS ACCRUED INTEREST FROM OCTOBER 11, 2019 TO YIELD 3.137% TO MATURITY..UDR INC - WILL REDEEM ALL $400 MILLION AGGREGATE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT OF ITS OUTSTANDING 4.625% SENIOR UNSECURED NOTES DUE JANUARY 10, 2022.'}{'symbol': 'UAL', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'UNITED AIRLINES LAUNCHES AVIATE, ITS NEW PILOT RECRUITMENT PROGRAM AND CAREER WEBSITE', 'text': 'OCT 3  - UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC <UAL.O>::UNITED AIRLINES - ANNOUNCED LAUNCH OF AVIATE, ITS NEW PILOT RECRUITMENT PROGRAM AND CAREER WEBSITE.UNITED AIRLINES - DUE TO RETIREMENTS, ATTRITION & PROJECTED GROWTH, CO ANTICIPATES HIRING MORE THAN 10,000 PILOTS BY 2029.'}{'symbol': 'UPS', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'UNITED PARCEL SERVICE, INC. PRESENTS AT STEPHENS NASHVILLE INVESTMENT CONFERENCE, NOV-13-2019', 'text': 'UNITED PARCEL SERVICE, INC. PRESENTS AT STEPHENS NASHVILLE INVESTMENT CONFERENCE, NOV-13-2019 . VENUE: OMNI NASHVILLE HOTEL, 250 FIFTH AVENUE S, NASHVILLE, TENNESSEE, UNITED STATES. SPEAKERS: ALDRED WILLIAMS, VP OF INVESTOR RELATIONS, KAREN MOTHNER, DIRECTOR OF INVESTOR RELATIONS.'}{'symbol': 'VRSK', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'VERISK LAUNCHES COURTSIDE', 'text': 'VERISK ANNOUNCED THE LAUNCH OF COURTSIDE, A LEGAL ANALYTICS SOLUTION THAT AGGREGATES AND SCORES THOUSANDS OF INSURANCE-RELATED COURT DECISIONS BY TOPIC TO HELP INSURERS RESPOND QUICKLY AND COST-EFFECTIVELY TO CASE LAW TRENDS. CASE LAW CHANGES CAN HAVE A PROFOUND IMPACT ACROSS THE INSURANCE VALUE CHAIN. THEY CAN AFFECT EVERYTHING FROM THE TYPES OF EXPOSURES CARRIERS ARE WILLING TO INSURE TO THEIR RESERVE ALLOCATION STRATEGIES. IN SOME CASES, COURT DECISIONS CAN INFLUENCE WHETHER AN INSURER CHOOSES TO WRITE A PARTICULAR CLASS OF BUSINESS IN A SPECIFIC JURISDICTION. BUT MONITORING, ANALYZING, AND INCORPORATING CASE LAW TRENDS INTO STRATEGIC DECISION MAKING CAN BE COSTLY AND TIME-CONSUMING. COURTSIDE CATEGORIZES LEGAL DECISIONS BY SEVERAL CRITERIA, INCLUDING TOPIC, BUSINESS CLASSIFICATION, AND CORRELATION BETWEEN TERMS APPEARING IN SELECT CASE LAW AND POLICY LANGUAGE. IT THEN APPLIES A SCORING MODEL TO HELP USERS GAUGE THE POTENTIAL IMPACT OF COURT DECISIONS ON THEIR INSUREDS’ BUSINESSES. COURTSIDE FEATURES A USER-FRIENDLY DASHBOARD, DATA EXTRACTION CAPABILITIES THAT ENABLE INSURERS TO DO THEIR OWN ANALYSIS, AND A LEGAL LIBRARY OF APPROXIMATELY 10,000 CASES. OPERATING AT THE INTERSECTION OF INSURTECH AND LEGALTECH, COURTSIDE GATHERS DECISIONS FROM MORE THAN 200 STATE APPELLATE AND SUPREME COURTS, AS WELL AS FEDERAL DISTRICT AND CIRCUIT COURTS TO PROVIDE ONGOING UPDATES AND INSIGHT FOR INSURERS.'}{'symbol': 'WAB', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'WABTEC CORPORATION, Q3 2019 EARNINGS CALL, OCT 31, 2019', 'text': 'WABTEC CORPORATION, Q3 2019 EARNINGS CALL, OCT 31, 2019'}{'symbol': 'WBA', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'WALGREENS BOOTS ALLIANCE, INC. PRESENTS AT GITEX TECHNOLOGY WEEK, OCT-08-2019 11:40 AM', 'text': 'WALGREENS BOOTS ALLIANCE, INC. PRESENTS AT GITEX TECHNOLOGY WEEK, OCT-08-2019 11:40 AM. VENUE: DUBAI, UNITED ARAB EMIRATES. SPEAKERS: VISH SANKARAN, CHIEF INNOVATION OFFICER.'}{'symbol': 'ZTS', 'date': '2019-10-02 22:30:00', 'title': 'ZOETIS INC. ANNOUNCES CEO CHANGES', 'text': 'ZOETIS INC. ANNOUNCED THAT KRISTIN PECK WILL SUCCEED JUAN RAMÓN ALAIX AS CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER, EFFECTIVE JANUARY 1, 2020, AND JOIN THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS, EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY. ALAIX, WHO HAS BEEN CEO OF ZOETIS SINCE ITS FORMATION IN 2012, HAS DECIDED TO RETIRE AS CEO EFFECTIVE DECEMBER 31, 2019. HE WILL ACT AS AN ADVISOR ON THE LEADERSHIP TRANSITION THROUGH DECEMBER 31, 2020. KRISTIN PECK WILL SUCCEED JUAN RAMÓN ALAIX AS CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER OF ZOETIS, EFFECTIVE JANUARY 1, 2020, AND JOIN THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS, EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY.'}